// Load buffering where one write's value comes from a division that is
// undefined unless the read returned 0 -- the model-dependent half of the pair.
//
// Source: the MRD line's numbered out-of-thin-air listings.
//
// listing27_allow.lit is the same program annotated [UB11] and asserts the
// opposite. Both are right: a model that exploits undefined behaviour may
// assume r2 = 0 (else 1 / !r2 divides by zero), fold the write to y := 1 and
// break the dependency, so the outcome is allowed; a model that does not keeps
// the dependency on r2 and the outcome is out of thin air.
//
// This file names no model, so it is checked under smrd, whose ubopt is false.
// It had a witness (#45) because Interpret applied the fold unconditionally --
// options.ubopt was in the table, set by no one and read by no one, so [UB11]
// and no annotation were indistinguishable and the pair could not both hold.
// 31 executions became 27.
x := 0; y := 0;
{
  r1 := y;
  x := r1
}|||{
  r2 := x;
  y := 1 / !r2
}
%% forbid (r1 = 1 && r2 = 1) []
